From c4f02314960e0876bec97183e3bb40c2add19796 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 22:19:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 20/47] vrend: do not export a fence descriptor a host only
 emulates

Creating an EGL native fence makes the GL driver submit a command buffer
and export a semaphore for every guest fence. An Apple host has no
kernel fence to hand out, so its driver emulates the descriptor, and the
per-fence command buffers pile up unrecycled while the guest keeps
fencing: a sample of a desktop GL host taken 30 s into a conformance run
shows 48000 live driver command allocators and 2.2 million driver
resource pools, several gigabytes of host memory, all created under
eglCreateSyncKHR.

The renderer only ever asks a fence whether its work has finished, and
the GL sync object answers that. Leave the native fence to the hosts
whose fence descriptor is a real one.
---
 src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
index 753e3e8..2c09dd6 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -7780,7 +7780,20 @@ int vrend_renderer_init(const struct vrend_if_cbs *cbs, uint32_t flags)
       vrend_state.use_external_blob = true;
 
 #ifdef HAVE_EPOXY_EGL_H
+   /* An EGL native fence asks the GL driver for a fence it can hand out as a
+    * file descriptor, which forces a real command-buffer submission and an
+    * exportable semaphore for every guest fence. An Apple host has no kernel
+    * fence to export, so its driver emulates the descriptor, and the
+    * per-fence command buffers it allocates are never recycled while the
+    * guest keeps fencing: a GL workload costs the host gigabytes within a
+    * minute. The GL sync object answers the only question this renderer asks
+    * of a fence -- has the work finished -- so use the native fence only
+    * where the descriptor is real.
+    */
    vrend_state.use_egl_fence = virgl_egl_supports_fences(egl);
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+   vrend_state.use_egl_fence = false;
+#endif
 #endif
 
    if (!vrend_check_no_error(vrend_state.ctx0)) {
